<title>DENMARK: Maersk Air denies media takeover talk.</title>
<headline>Maersk Air denies media takeover talk.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Danish Maersk Air, a unit of energy and shipping group A.P. Moeller, on Monday dismissed local media rumours of plans to take over Norway's Braathens SAFE and Deutsche BA, a German subsidiary of British Airways.</p>
<p>&quot;These rumours are absolutely unfounded,&quot; a Maersk Air spokeswoman told Reuters.</p>
<p>The Danish business daily Erhvervsbladet reported unconfirmed rumours and anonymous sources as saying that Maersk planned to acquire the Norwegian and Anglo-German airlines as part of a strategic plan to intensify competition with Scandinavian Airlines System (SAS). --Soeren Linding Jakobsen, Copenhagen newsroom +45-33969653</p>
